---
import Base from "../layouts/Base.astro";
---
<Base>
  <section class="page">
    <h1>Sacraments</h1>

    <h2>Becoming Catholic</h2>
    <p>God has been stirring something in your heart. We are thankful you are looking for the next step.</p>
    <p>Your first step is a conversation. You can ask questions and discern from there. If you were baptized Catholic and still need Confession, Eucharist, or Confirmation, start with the same call.</p>
    <p>Those who want to enter the Church continue through the Order of Christian Initiation of Adults. That process can take several months or longer. Someone already baptized is not baptized again.</p>
    <h3>Who it is for</h3>
    <ul>
      <li>Adults who have never been baptized</li>
      <li>Adults baptized in another Christian church</li>
      <li>Catholics who still need Confession, Eucharist, or Confirmation</li>
    </ul>
    <h3>The process</h3>
    <ul>
      <li>Inquiry: questions and getting acquainted with the Church</li>
      <li>Catechumenate: instruction after the Rite of Acceptance</li>
      <li>Purification: preparation during Lent</li>
      <li>Sacraments, usually at the Easter Vigil</li>
      <li>Mystagogy: the weeks after initiation</li>
    </ul>
    <p>Contact Sarah Nelson, (719) 542-9248 ext. 121, snelson@ctkpueblo.org.</p>
    <p>Older children go through Sharlyn Garduno, ext. 114, sgarduno@ctkpueblo.org.</p>

    <h2>Baptism</h2>
    <p>Infants through age 17. Contact Leslie Soell, ext. 113, lsoell@ctkpueblo.org.</p>
    <h3>Baptism requirements</h3>
    <ul>
      <li>Birth certificate</li>
      <li>Parish registration</li>
      <li>Petition for baptism</li>
      <li>Meeting with the pastor</li>
      <li>Godparent paperwork</li>
    </ul>
    <h3>Godparent requirements</h3>
    <ul>
      <li>Practicing and fully initiated Catholic</li>
      <li>At least 16 years old and not the parent</li>
      <li>One godfather and one godmother</li>
      <li>If married, the marriage must be recognized by the Church</li>
      <li>A copy of each godparent's confirmation certificate</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>First Reconciliation</h2>
    <p>Second grade, age 7, or older, after one year of religious formation. A parent attends with the child. Contact Leslie Soell, ext. 113, lsoell@ctkpueblo.org.</p>
    <h3>Preparation</h3>
    <ul>
      <li>Sessions run 9:15–10:45 a.m.</li>
      <li>A parent or guardian attends with the child</li>
      <li>One year of religious formation before the sessions</li>
      <li>Children also stay in regular formation</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>First Eucharist</h2>
    <p>Second grade, age 7, or older. A parent attends with the child. Children receive at a regular weekend Mass, usually in early May. Contact Leslie Soell, ext. 113, lsoell@ctkpueblo.org.</p>
    <h3>Preparation</h3>
    <ul>
      <li>Sessions run 9:15–10:45 a.m.</li>
      <li>A parent or guardian attends with the child</li>
      <li>First Eucharist is celebrated at a weekend Mass</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>Confirmation</h2>
    <p>Incoming 7th and 8th grade, and high school youth who still need the sacrament, after one year of formation. Contact Aden Casarez, ext. 114, or Sarah Nelson, ext. 121, for adults.</p>
    <h3>Requirements</h3>
    <ul>
      <li>One year of religious formation first</li>
      <li>Monthly preparation sessions</li>
      <li>A copy of the baptismal certificate</li>
      <li>A sponsor who is a fully initiated Catholic and at least 16</li>
      <li>A confirmation saint</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>Marriage</h2>
    <p>Couples should call as soon as they are engaged. Contact Sarah Nelson, (719) 542-9248 ext. 121, snelson@ctkpueblo.org.</p>

    <h2>Anointing of the Sick</h2>
    <p>For baptized Catholics, at least 7, who are seriously ill. Do not wait until the point of death. Contact Sharlyn Garduno, ext. 114, sgarduno@ctkpueblo.org.</p>
    <h3>Who it is for</h3>
    <ul>
      <li>A serious or chronic illness</li>
      <li>An older person whose health is weakening</li>
      <li>A person preparing for surgery</li>
      <li>A person suffering from addiction or mental illness</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>Funerals</h2>
    <p>Families call Fr. Zaldy Norba, (719) 542-9248 ext. 116, znorba@ctkpueblo.org.</p>
  </section>
</Base>

